    A001["<div class='arg'><b>A001 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed's choice at the Sept FOMC is between a hike and risking a large bond spike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond price action, including post Friday's CPI, shows the bond likes orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>Q:</b> The Fed faces a simple choice at the Sept FOMC.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC001 - Fed holds at Sept FOMC</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC002 - Fed hikes at Sept FOMC</b></span></div></div>"]
    A002["<div class='arg'><b>A002 · OBSERVATION</b><div class='core obs'><span>The priced probability of a Sept FOMC hike is up sharply in recent weeks.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The sharp shift in Fed pricing was catalyzed by the Warsh Jackson Hole (JH) speech.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The sharp shift in Fed pricing was catalyzed by stronger labor data.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The sharp shift in Fed pricing was catalyzed by stronger inflation data.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A003["<div class='arg'><b>A003 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed hikes 25bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A001 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c obs'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A002 - OBSERVATION</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Rate pricing is firmly in the zone to support a hike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's CPI data all but lock in a rate hike this week.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Chairman Warsh's Jackson Hole remarks have raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Current market pricing has raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's twist flattening of the Treasury curve provides further justification for a hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh understands bond risk with a Sept hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Others at the Fed understand bond risk with a Sept hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Trump admin understands bond risk with a Sept hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A004["<div class='arg'><b>A004 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The key question is the Warsh presser.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The rate reaction to a Fed hike depends on the mix of Fed communications.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> In responding to questions about the policy path going forward, Warsh faces a balancing act.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC003 - Hawkish presser, Jackson Hole Warsh</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC004 - Dovish presser, July FOMC Warsh</b></span></div></div>"]
    A005["<div class='arg'><b>A005 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The hawkish hike supports the author's constructive long end asset swap spread view.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower growth risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower inflation risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Enhanced Fed credibility supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A006["<div class='arg'><b>A006 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh delivers a hawkish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A003 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A004 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Sept FOMC communications lean hawkish.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The hawkish hike challenges the author's prior bias for lower belly rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> <b>A005 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A007["<div class='arg'><b>A007 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>IM:</b> The USD trades more-or-less sideways into year-end (ex-JPY).</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A008["<div class='arg'><b>A008 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A007 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> With evolving expectations, considerable two-way risk remains for the USD at Wednesday's meeting.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>RI:</b> Chair Warsh's aversion to forward guidance makes the bullish USD case challenging.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC005 - Bullish USD: hawkish hike and SEP</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC006 - Bearish USD: Fed holds</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC007 - Bearish USD: hike with muddled messaging</b></span></div></div>"]
    SC001["<div class='arg'><b>SC001 · Scenario · Fed holds at Sept FOMC</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed surprisingly holds.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed risks a sharp and disorderly UST long end move.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> US 30Y rapidly tests 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a material front end rate decline.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a sharp twist steepening of the curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Over time, the 30Y increases towards 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Investor confidence in the Fed is limited.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Treasury buybacks prove futile to stop the UST long end move.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed hold represents an unprecedented dovish hold (using FOMC OIS data back to '07).</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A larger market move comes from a Fed hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC002["<div class='arg'><b>SC002 · Scenario · Fed hikes at Sept FOMC</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>THEN:</b> The language around inflation in the FOMC statement is modified to rationalize the Sep hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>THEN:</b> The 2026 median dot shows 50bp of hikes this year.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The 2026 median dot implies another rate increase in Oct or Dec.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>THEN:</b> Chair Warsh fields questions about the policy path going forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>THEN:</b> Gov. Waller dissents.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC003["<div class='arg'><b>SC003 · Scenario · Hawkish presser, Jackson Hole Warsh</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh continues to sound inflation impatient.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh suggests recent data does not imply an adequate disinflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market raises the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market pulls forward hike timing.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Total hikes are 100bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Hikes by end '26 are 60-65bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The hawkish presser sees 2Y rates rise 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The hawkish presser sees 30Y rates lower by 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are lower due to a more credible Fed return to orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Risk is challenged.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC004["<div class='arg'><b>SC004 · Scenario · Dovish presser, July FOMC Warsh</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh implies few hikes to follow.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market reduces the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market pushes out hike timing.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dovish presser sees 2Y rates lower by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dovish presser sees 30Y rates higher by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are higher due to confusion about Warsh policy direction or reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A bigger Bessent #quot;house#quot; is needed for the bond.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Markets once again question the Fed's commitment to the 2% inflation target.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A larger market move comes from a dovish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC005["<div class='arg'><b>SC005 · Scenario · Bullish USD: hawkish hike and SEP</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The SEP shows broadening support for additional hikes (relative to the June SEP).</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Inflation forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Chair Warsh himself, intentionally or unintentionally, offers some indication that a more prolonged campaign is necessary to return inflation on the path to 2%.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed hikes at least 100bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed brings current expectations forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The USD is supported.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC006["<div class='arg'><b>SC006 · Scenario · Bearish USD: Fed holds</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed opts to hold in the face of sticky inflation and market pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC007["<div class='arg'><b>SC007 · Scenario · Bearish USD: hike with muddled messaging</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Messaging muddles the reaction function further.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The broader committee (outside of the already identified hawkish members) appears reluctant to tighten policy in the current environment.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The USD softens with dovish or non-committal language from Warsh.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The USD falls in tandem with rising back-end yields.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A more restrained SEP dot-plot weighs on the dollar.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]

